# DevSense Laravel Playground - AI Agent Rules

Always refer to the project context files before planning or executing changes.

## 1. Project Stack & Execution
- **Core Stack**: Laravel 13, PHP 8.5, Vite + Vue 3, Tailwind CSS v4, PostgreSQL, Redis, Meilisearch.
- **Commands**: Always run commands via **Laravel Sail** (`./vendor/bin/sail ...`) from the repository root:
  - Run Tests: `./vendor/bin/sail test` or `./vendor/bin/sail php artisan test`
  - Artisan: `./vendor/bin/sail php artisan <command>`
  - Composer: `./vendor/bin/sail composer <command>`
  - Node/NPM: `./vendor/bin/sail npm <command>`

## 2. Project Rules & Guidelines
Follow the guidelines established in the MDC rule files:
1. **Context Initialization**: Review [.cursor/project-progress.md](file:///.cursor/project-progress.md) to understand current status, roadmap, and instructions.
2. **Read Context Rule**: Refer to [.cursor/rules/read-dot-cursor-context.mdc](file:///.cursor/rules/read-dot-cursor-context.mdc) (always active).
3. **Content Writing Standards**: Refer to [.cursor/rules/writing-guidelines.mdc](file:///.cursor/rules/writing-guidelines.mdc) (applies to `resources/content/**/*.md`).
   - Use the specific technical article skeleton.
   - Strip AI watermarks and metadata from images.
   - Configure SEO/AEO FAQ metadata in front matter.
   - Use relative localized link structures.

## 3. General Best Practices
- **Documentation**: Maintain all existing comments, docstrings, and type hints. Avoid leaving excessive comments in the code; if code comments are necessary, they MUST be written exclusively in English.
- **Testing**: Ensure that all changes are verified by running `./vendor/bin/sail test` before finishing tasks.
- **Theme Support**: Always ensure all newly added or modified frontend components (e.g., modals, inputs, buttons, tables) support all three active themes (`light`, `dark`, `nord`) by utilizing CSS variables from `base/_variables.scss` (e.g., `var(--bg-color)`, `var(--text-color)`, `var(--page-bg)`, `var(--border-color)`, `var(--primary-color)`). Never hardcode theme-specific colors.
- **Commit Messages**: At the end of every completed task or block of work, always propose a recommended Git commit message.
- **Communication**: Always write summaries of the completed work and updates to the USER in Russian.

